From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:13:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 091/112] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250-motorola-nairo: Keep the
 splash display powered

Without consumers, the display clock controller powers the MDSS GDSC
off as soon as it probes, which blanks the screen under simpledrm. List
the GDSC and the clocks the scanout needs in the simple-framebuffer
node, so simpledrm holds them.

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index 4377c2d2a..52bea5d87 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -66,6 +66,17 @@ &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>,
 					<&mmss_noc MASTER_MDP_PORT1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
 			peak-kBps = <6400000>;
+			/*
+			 * Keep the display engine powered and clocked while the
+			 * firmware framebuffer is in use: without consumers, the
+			 * display clock controller powers the MDSS domain off.
+			 */
+			power-domains = <&dispcc MDSS_GDSC>;
+			clocks = <&gcc GCC_DISP_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_DISP_HF_AXI_CLK>,
+				 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_MDP_CLK>,
+				 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>;
 		};
 	};
 
